* The inducing map is a group homomorphism of the character groups (Mathlib changeLevel : DirichletCharacter R n ->* DirichletCharacter R m).

s1::simp1 |- ( ( N e. NN /\ M e. NN /\ N || M ) -> N e. NN )
s2::simp2 |- ( ( N e. NN /\ M e. NN /\ N || M ) -> M e. NN )
s3::eqid |- ( Base ` ( DChr ` N ) ) = ( Base ` ( DChr ` N ) )
s4::eqid |- ( Base ` ( DChr ` M ) ) = ( Base ` ( DChr ` M ) )
s5::eqid |- ( +g ` ( DChr ` N ) ) = ( +g ` ( DChr ` N ) )
s6::eqid |- ( +g ` ( DChr ` M ) ) = ( +g ` ( DChr ` M ) )
s7::eqid |- ( DChr ` N ) = ( DChr ` N )
s8:s7:dchrabl |- ( N e. NN -> ( DChr ` N ) e. Abel )
s9:s1,s8:syl |- ( ( N e. NN /\ M e. NN /\ N || M ) -> ( DChr ` N ) e. Abel )
s10::eqid |- ( DChr ` M ) = ( DChr ` M )
s11:s10:dchrabl |- ( M e. NN -> ( DChr ` M ) e. Abel )
